# THE REACTION BENCHMARK -- hand-typed, pipe-separated, one row per case.
#
#   case | class | reactants | products | coproducts | note
#
# What it is for. The catalog scores NAMED ROUTES, and a template that works on
# one substrate pair scores the same there as one that works on five hundred.
# This file scores GENERALITY: each class is tried on substrates it was never
# written from, and a template that only knows its own step fails here.
#
# case        class/short-name, unique.
# class       a route_steps.psv reaction class. A template is graded on the
#             classes it claims, so a class name the catalog does not use is
#             one no template can pass yet -- which is allowed, and counted.
# reactants   ' + '-separated SMILES, spelled the way this repo spells them:
#             [H][H], O=O, [C-]#[O+], ions as ions. Water, hydronium and
#             hydroxide are always available as the medium and need not be
#             listed unless they are consumed.
# products    the textbook major product(s), flat (no stereo). ALL must come
#             back from one application of one template for a pass.
# coproducts  the rest of the balanced equation. Not required of a template
#             (a row may write H2O2 where this writes water); used only so
#             tools/benchmark.py can check the case balances uniquely.
# note        why this case is here, when it is not obvious.
#
# Rules, all enforced by tools/benchmark.py --check:
#   - every SMILES parses, and reactants -> products + coproducts balances by
#     element and charge with every coefficient between 1 and 4;
#   - no case is a catalog step of the same class (a held-out set that
#     contains its own training row measures nothing);
#   - a case never names stereochemistry.
# Each outcome is the standard textbook one; the balance check guards the
# typing, not the chemistry, so a regiochemistry claim is stated in `note`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- family-covered
